From: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: trigger: netdev: qualify activity with the link mode

With link_100 and RX/TX enabled, a gigabit link correctly leaves an LED
off until the first packet. Activity polling then blinks it regardless
of speed, and the inverted one-shot restores it to on because a link
mode is selected. On the XG6846B both the green gigabit and amber 100M
indicators therefore light up during gigabit traffic and can remain on.

Start software activity polling only when the configured link modes
match. State changes already cancel pending work before resetting the
baseline, and a matching link event starts polling again. Keep LEDs
configured for activity alone working without a link mode, and leave
hardware offload unchanged.
Use the same link-mode mask to select the one-shot polarity.

Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
---
--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@
 #include "../leds.h"
 
 #define NETDEV_LED_DEFAULT_INTERVAL	50
+#define NETDEV_LED_LINK_MODES		GENMASK(TRIGGER_NETDEV_FULL_DUPLEX, \
+						TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK)
 
 /*
  * Configurable sysfs attributes:
@@ -141,6 +143,15 @@
 					   led_cdev->blink_brightness);
 		else
 			led_set_brightness(led_cdev, LED_OFF);
+
+		/*
+		 * Link modes also qualify activity blinking. Otherwise traffic
+		 * blinks LEDs for other speeds and the inverted one-shot leaves
+		 * them on. Callers cancel pending work before updating state;
+		 * a later matching link event will restart activity polling.
+		 */
+		if (!blink_on && (trigger_data->mode & NETDEV_LED_LINK_MODES))
+			return;
 
 		/* If we are looking for RX/TX start periodically
 		 * checking stats
@@ -661,15 +672,7 @@
 	if (trigger_data->last_activity != new_activity) {
 		led_stop_software_blink(trigger_data->led_cdev);
 
-		invert = test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_10, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_100, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_1000, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_2500, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_5000, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_LINK_10000, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_HALF_DUPLEX, &trigger_data->mode) ||
-			 test_bit(TRIGGER_NETDEV_FULL_DUPLEX, &trigger_data->mode);
+		invert = !!(trigger_data->mode & NETDEV_LED_LINK_MODES);
 		interval = jiffies_to_msecs(
 				atomic_read(&trigger_data->interval));
 		/* base state is ON (link present) */
